{"agent":"lane-sec-policy-contact","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"Given a valid but longer contact such as `export.security_contact = \"https://example.com/report?token= [REDACTED] + \"a\" * 300`, `_reporting` calls `one_line(cfg.export.security_contact, 300)`, so the contact published in SECURITY.md is truncated to the 300-character limit rather than being the configured value. The knob accepts an arbitrarily long string and the config docs say the contact is written as given and exempt from redaction; silently cutting a reporting URL/email to 300 characters can make the published contact unusable and may also break any exact-value redaction exemption that relies on the configured text appearing unchanged.","digest":"7daf9c68025468fb","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/export/kind_security.py:_reporting","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/export/kind_security.py:_reporting"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The new “exempt the contact” logic splits the whole rendered body on the configured `security_contact` string before redaction, so any other secret that contains that contact as a substring is broken into pieces that may no longer match the redactor’s patterns. For example, with `export.security_contact = \"example.com\"` and an export body containing the sensitive email `[REDACTED:email]`, line 44 splits the text into `\"alice@\"` and `\"\"`. The redactor would normally redact the full email address, but after the split it only sees `\"alice@\"`, which is not a complete email pattern, so the local part is emitted unredacted. The intent was to exempt the reporting contact itself, not to disable redaction for unrelated secrets that merely contain the contact string.","digest":"42ab5734f3128ef4","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/export/safe.py:44","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/export/safe.py:44"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":30891,"diff_sha":"bfeb42c7e195e791233cb281f781adcf7e42ace4a503c4bf602e6b2c2e3c19e3","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/SEC-policy-contact","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":380.1,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"40761649136c5448","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SEC-policy-contact.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T185936Z-f0eee03c.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"reviewed_head":"df7043c042d013e28cc9b4285cad6ebab41e742a","reviewed_paths":{"SECURITY.md":"100644 4f64fa3d4dcecd479d3a2ed4619862728d422397","ddflow/config_sections/export.py":"100644 a921d35128c44abb873fcbb626627d435836fe65","ddflow/services/export/kind_security.py":"100644 70f2e9f4a2c8cd566d4484ca3ae998dda37d9c74","ddflow/services/export/safe.py":"100644 9f23e6ebe2fde405662b0a54d75df3dfed0cf209","ddflow/services/export/select.py":"100644 a153c2ccffd7b50c45f311d5892b8cc38fa41b06","ddflow/templates/export/security.md.j2":"100644 1612f86e560ce3e79940a405f98ce623a98a1c8f","ddflow/templates/prompts/help/export.md":"100644 f70064929b58d9b47d434747e1db67f75b8ecd3b","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.export.security_contact.toml":"100644 6934b1da4149ec45defdce0e98435640153b71ec","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.export.security_response_days.toml":"100644 28b8d663b530f06ba69ca5781cb4116084ef50d2","docs/guide/customisation.md":"100644 96c21335e2736668a860890ec0baf6c076954a58","tests/test_export_security.py":"100644 797a726f1d82e4eaa1ab2759f48d20a8de4a6db4","tests/test_security_doc_contact.py":"100644 09995218c71500d2c515e8c3fe8d4dec049fa547"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/export/kind_security.py:_reporting","ddflow/services/export/safe.py:44"],"tree_sha":"df7043c042d0+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":2},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"ebdff3086be317f9505d9efe0","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":195779,"schema":1,"subject":"SEC-policy-contact","ts":"2026-11-13T19:05:58.335297Z"}
