{"agent":"lane-sec-policy-contact","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The contact exemption is implemented by splitting the rendered text on the exact configured `security_contact` and redacting only the pieces between occurrences. That exempts the configured substring wherever it appears, including inside a larger token that should still be redacted. For example, if `export.security_contact = \"[REDACTED:email]\"` and the rendered body contains the different address `[REDACTED:email]`, `text.split(keep)` yields `[\"not\", \"\"]`; neither piece contains a complete email address, so the redactor leaves both unchanged and the join returns `[REDACTED:email]` unredacted. The intended behavior is to leave only the configured contact visible while still redacting other email addresses, so this can leak redactable email addresses that contain the contact as a substring.","digest":"aee3e14ec5d5eb5d","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/export/safe.py:redact_export_text","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/export/safe.py:redact_export_text"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The new aggregation assumes `red.text(part).counts` is always a mapping, but the same file exposes `redaction_attrs(counts: Mapping[str, int] | None)` and documents a `redacted=off` header state. If the export redactor is disabled and the security body contains the configured contact, the redaction result used here can have `counts=None`, so the loop `for kind, n in part.counts.items()` raises `AttributeError` instead of returning the disabled-redaction result. Even if the disabled result uses an empty mapping rather than `None`, the code drops the original disabled/`None` state and reports ordinary zero redactions rather than `redacted=off`.","digest":"1fd5a4e453c58059","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/export/safe.py:redact_export_text","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/export/safe.py:redact_export_text"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The guide's total knob count is bumped from 675 to 744, but this change introduces only two knobs (`export.security_contact` and `export.security_response_days`, each with its own `knob_added` upgrade note). If the previous documented count matched the registry, the correct post-change count is 677; the line now claims 744, so a user comparing the documented total with `ddflow config --list` / the knob registry after this change gets a number off by 69.","digest":"7e94cf7c47e0ad63","family":"alibaba","location":"docs/guide/customisation.md:121","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"docs/guide/customisation.md:121"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":30891,"diff_sha":"bfeb42c7e195e791233cb281f781adcf7e42ace4a503c4bf602e6b2c2e3c19e3","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/SEC-policy-contact","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":812.0,"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"451a6b018174fd3e","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SEC-policy-contact.critic.[REDACTED:name].20261113T190600Z-1ee2f119.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"reviewed_head":"df7043c042d013e28cc9b4285cad6ebab41e742a","reviewed_paths":{"SECURITY.md":"100644 4f64fa3d4dcecd479d3a2ed4619862728d422397","ddflow/config_sections/export.py":"100644 a921d35128c44abb873fcbb626627d435836fe65","ddflow/services/export/kind_security.py":"100644 70f2e9f4a2c8cd566d4484ca3ae998dda37d9c74","ddflow/services/export/safe.py":"100644 9f23e6ebe2fde405662b0a54d75df3dfed0cf209","ddflow/services/export/select.py":"100644 a153c2ccffd7b50c45f311d5892b8cc38fa41b06","ddflow/templates/export/security.md.j2":"100644 1612f86e560ce3e79940a405f98ce623a98a1c8f","ddflow/templates/prompts/help/export.md":"100644 f70064929b58d9b47d434747e1db67f75b8ecd3b","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.export.security_contact.toml":"100644 6934b1da4149ec45defdce0e98435640153b71ec","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.export.security_response_days.toml":"100644 28b8d663b530f06ba69ca5781cb4116084ef50d2","docs/guide/customisation.md":"100644 96c21335e2736668a860890ec0baf6c076954a58","tests/test_export_security.py":"100644 797a726f1d82e4eaa1ab2759f48d20a8de4a6db4","tests/test_security_doc_contact.py":"100644 09995218c71500d2c515e8c3fe8d4dec049fa547"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/export/safe.py:redact_export_text","ddflow/services/export/safe.py:redact_export_text","docs/guide/customisation.md:121"],"tree_sha":"d9c3f44f533e+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":2},"gate":"critic","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"ec3f049576f68fe53e49b2ff7","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":195952,"schema":1,"subject":"SEC-policy-contact","ts":"2026-11-13T19:19:34.762636Z"}
